A short answer, temperature=0, six runs
  distinct answers: 1 of 6
  lengths:          [43]
  first 70 chars:   'Midwest revenue declined by 53% in Q3 2024.'

A long one, temperature=0, six runs
  distinct answers: 6 of 6
  lengths:          [737, 752, 756, 767, 796, 816]
  first 70 chars:   'Midwest revenue fell 53% in Q3 2024 primarily because our largest acco'

temperature=0 means 'always pick the most likely next token'. When one token is
far ahead of the others, that is stable. Over hundreds of tokens, some position
eventually has two near-equal candidates, and floating-point arithmetic on
different hardware breaks the tie differently. The longer the output, the more
chances for that to happen.

So: temperature=0 is a strong nudge, not a contract. Design as though the model
may answer differently tomorrow, because one day it will.
